WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.925 --> 00:00:19.151
It Saturday, and Katie Donovan sat on the kitchen floor petting Magoo, the family dog.

2
00:00:20.292 --> 00:00:23.873
Her twin sister, Joy, was at the big round table, waiting for a snack.

3
00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:28.895
Grandpa, the best cook in the family, had just baked brownies.

4
00:00:31.416 --> 00:00:32.077
"Mmm," said Katie.

5
00:00:32.097 --> 00:00:34.018
"I love brownies!"

6
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:40.444
Just then Mom looked toward the County Road and said, "The mail truck is coming, girls.

7
00:00:40.804 --> 00:00:41.785
It's turning the corner."

8
00:00:42.766 --> 00:00:43.667
Katie jumped up.

9
00:00:43.687 --> 00:00:45.148
"Let's go, Magoo!"

10
00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.672
She and the hound raced through the house and out the front door.

11
00:00:50.253 --> 00:00:53.015
Magoo followed Katie all the way down the driveway.

12
00:00:54.977 --> 00:00:58.260
Katie hardly ever got any mail, except birthday cards.

13
00:00:58.772 --> 00:01:01.434
And those were sent to Katie and Joy Donovan.

14
00:01:02.614 --> 00:01:05.656
But both girls still liked to collect the mail when it came.

15
00:01:06.776 --> 00:01:09.898
The mail truck rumbled to a stop at 10 Blackberry Road.

16
00:01:11.119 --> 00:01:12.900
The mailman leaned out of the window.

17
00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:14.200
"Hello, Magoo!"

18
00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.702
he called and gave the mail to Katie.

19
00:01:16.722 --> 00:01:19.743
"Hello, Jeff," said Katie.

20
00:01:20.924 --> 00:01:22.245
Jeff looked at her closely.

21
00:01:22.265 --> 00:01:23.685
"Which twin are you?"

22
00:01:24.046 --> 00:01:24.586
he asked.

23
00:01:25.726 --> 00:01:26.607
Katie sighed.

24
00:01:26.627 --> 00:01:28.208
"I'm KATIE."

25
00:01:29.996 --> 00:01:32.837
"I always get you two mixed-up," said Jeff.

26
00:01:33.437 --> 00:01:35.117
Then he drove off down the road.

27
00:01:35.137 --> 00:01:41.679
"We're totally different mumbled Katie as the mail truck disappeared in a cloud of dust.

28
00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.600
Katie liked having a sister who was her identical twin.

29
00:01:47.041 --> 00:01:50.702
But she hated it when people mixed them up, which happened all the time.

30
00:01:50.722 --> 00:01:54.043
"You know which one I am, don't you, Magoo?"

31
00:01:54.643 --> 00:01:55.463
whispered Katie.

32
00:01:56.103 --> 00:01:57.323
Magoo sniffed her hand.

33
00:01:57.343 --> 00:01:59.144
"That's right.

34
00:01:59.648 --> 00:02:01.889
Joy and I smell different, don't we?"

35
00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.091
The house smelled like brownies.

36
00:02:06.111 --> 00:02:08.512
"Mail delivery!"

37
00:02:08.832 --> 00:02:09.732
Katie called out.

38
00:02:10.272 --> 00:02:12.033
She read the name on the first envelope.

39
00:02:12.053 --> 00:02:15.975
"For John Donovan—from Sunshine Seed Company."

40
00:02:15.995 --> 00:02:18.756
"Great!" said Grandpa.

41
00:02:18.776 --> 00:02:20.017
"My corn seeds!"

42
00:02:20.517 --> 00:02:22.638
Grandpa would be planting the garden soon.

43
00:02:22.658 --> 00:02:28.040
"Here's a letter for Debra Donovan," said Katie, flipping through the mail.

44
00:02:29.168 --> 00:02:31.669
Mom was looking at a book about Missouri birds.

45
00:02:31.689 --> 00:02:33.870
"Thanks, honey," she said.

46
00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:36.971
"And for Steve A.

47
00:02:37.031 --> 00:02:39.452
Donovan—the new Green Zine!"

48
00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:40.933
exclaimed Katie.

49
00:02:42.073 --> 00:02:44.434
This was a magazine all about recycling.

50
00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:47.235
Dad owned the Willow Creek Recycling Center.

51
00:02:47.255 --> 00:02:50.817
"The rest is junk mail," said Katie.

52
00:02:51.397 --> 00:02:52.958
"Nothing for us today, Joy.

53
00:02:53.618 --> 00:02:55.659
Unless you want a chicken catalog!

54
00:02:56.039 --> 00:02:58.400
It's from a place called the Cackle Farm."

55
00:02:58.928 --> 00:02:59.969
She said with a grin.

56
00:02:59.989 --> 00:03:04.692
"Okay," said Joy as Katie grabbed a brownie from the table.

57
00:03:04.712 --> 00:03:08.315
"Okay?" echoed Katie in surprise.

58
00:03:08.335 --> 00:03:12.578
"Okay, I'll look at the catalog," repeated Joy.

59
00:03:12.598 --> 00:03:15.600
"Really?" Katie handed it to her.

60
00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.481
"You're interested in chickens?"

61
00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:20.963
"Yep." Joy flipped through the catalog.

62
00:03:20.983 --> 00:03:25.427
"Hey, I didn't know chickens came in all these colors," she said.

63
00:03:25.447 --> 00:03:27.208
"Look at this one, Katie!"

64
00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.001
"I don't like chickens," Katie said.

65
00:03:31.021 --> 00:03:32.382
"You like them."

66
00:03:32.402 --> 00:03:36.064
"You're no fun sometimes," Joy complained.

67
00:03:37.125 --> 00:03:38.345
Katie ignored her sister.

68
00:03:38.926 --> 00:03:42.547
Instead she followed Dad, who was carrying a bucket out to the compost bin.

69
00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:50.752
she asked slowly, "how can you tell I'm Katie and not Joy?"

70
00:03:50.772 --> 00:03:53.673
"Oh, that's easy.

71
00:03:53.693 --> 00:03:57.395
I just Well Then Dad grinned.

72
00:03:57.415 --> 00:03:58.176
"I know.

73
00:03:58.508 --> 00:03:59.289
Your freckles!

74
00:03:59.789 --> 00:04:01.550
You have fourteen freckles on your nose.

75
00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:02.771
Joy has twelve!"

76
00:04:02.791 --> 00:04:05.252
"Oh, Dad!"

77
00:04:05.672 --> 00:04:06.393
Katie moaned.

78
00:04:06.413 --> 00:04:08.334
"You don't believe me?

79
00:04:08.654 --> 00:04:09.354
Go count them!"

80
00:04:10.655 --> 00:04:13.056
Katie rolled her eyes and walked back inside.

81
00:04:14.217 --> 00:04:15.578
Her father was teasing her.

82
00:04:16.138 --> 00:04:19.280
He didn't understand that sometimes it was hard to be a twin.

83
00:04:20.441 --> 00:04:22.242
Joy was still looking at the catalog.

84
00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:26.164
"We can buy these chickens when they are tiny chicks and raise them."

85
00:04:27.584 --> 00:04:28.785
"Then what would we do?

86
00:04:29.105 --> 00:04:30.246
Make fried chicken?

87
00:04:30.546 --> 00:04:32.187
HA!" joked Katie.

88
00:04:32.207 --> 00:04:34.308
"We wouldn't eat them!"

89
00:04:34.688 --> 00:04:35.248
Joy said.

90
00:04:35.268 --> 00:04:36.569
"We'd eat their eggs!"

91
00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.011
"What's wrong with the eggs from Tucker's Grocery?"

92
00:04:40.591 --> 00:04:41.172
asked Katie.

93
00:04:42.633 --> 00:04:43.393
Joy made a face.

94
00:04:43.413 --> 00:04:47.515
"Chickens are fun, Katie—not like you right now!"

95
00:04:48.656 --> 00:04:49.577
Katie looked away.

96
00:04:50.157 --> 00:04:52.638
She knew she was being a little mean to her sister.

97
00:04:53.079 --> 00:04:55.260
But for some reason, she couldn't help it today.
